  "body": "Refs #1448. Part of #1448.\n\nDepends on #3324 (the shared mechanism). Do not start before #3324 is merged. The `blocked` label goes when #3324 is closed.\n\n## What happens\n\nPlasma Profile has `lead_in`, `lead_out` and `reversed` (`crates/app/src/operation/types/plasma.rs:45-49`), but no pick. The user cannot set the pierce point or the place where the cut ends. On a visible edge, the pierce mark then sits where the generator puts it. No waterjet kind is on `main` yet: `Family::Waterjet` (`crates/app/src/operation/kinds.rs:1779`) has no operation.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Start: the pierce point is at the lead-in start that lands on the projection of the pick on the profile.\n- Exit: the lead-out and the cancel point (the torch off) are at the projection of the exit pick, after the overburn.\n- A waterjet kind that `main` adds later takes the same pick through the shared mechanism. This issue holds that rule. The waterjet slice is done when the kind exists.\n\nSeam: the arm `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs:127`; the lead rule in `plasma.rs:16` (lead longer than the kerf).\n\n## Laws a pick must keep (refused by name, never moved)\n\n- The pierce point is in the scrap, not on the part that stays.\n- The lead room and the kerf compensation hold at the pick.\n- The small-hole rule (`small_hole_dia`) and the overburn keep their laws.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A pin test shows the pierce at the start pick and the cancel at the exit pick, with golden CL.\n- A pin test shows a pick whose pierce falls on the part refused by name.\n- Undo and redo restore the previous path. MCP `edit_operation` sets the picks.\n- Every shipped plasma golden without a pick is byte-identical.\n\nSafety floor: this changes toolpaths and posted G-code.\n",
